                "added": [
                    "#Manage your emotions. Every one of us (including adults) sometimes gets angry, frustrated, whiny, or stressed out. There is no way to deny or avoid these emotions and it would be unhealthy to do so anyway. However, you can work on [[Understand-Your-Emotions|recognizing]] and managing your emotions more effectively.<ref>https://www.psychologytoday.com/us/blog/blamestorming/201708/how-to-manage-your-emotions</ref>[[Image:Be a Good Child Step 2 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Treat others like you want to be treated.  Many people call this the “golden rule,” and it really is a valuable rule to live by.  For children, acting toward your parents, friends and family, and other people with this guide in mind demonstrates thoughtfulness and maturity on your part.<ref>https://www.psychologytoday.com/us/blog/the-heart-and-science-of-attachment/202108/why-we-treat-others-as-we-have-been-treated</ref>[[Image:Be a Good Child Step 7 Version 2.jpg|center]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Manage your emotions. Every one of us (including adults) sometimes gets angry, frustrated, whiny, or stressed out. There is no way to deny or avoid these emotions and it would be unhealthy to do so anyway. However, you can work on [[Understand-Your-Emotions|recognizing]] and managing your emotions more effectively.<ref>https://www.psychologytoday.com/intl/blog/blamestorming/201708/how-manage-your-emotions</ref>[[Image:Be a Good Child Step 2 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
