        {
            "id": "17670838",
            "user": "CelesteTu",
            "timestamp": "21:44, 24 June 2015",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(2,924 bytes)",
            "change": -469,
            "summary": "(cleaning up)",
            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "deletion",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Honor your parents. Don't lie to them, and don't do any sneaky stuff; because they know what you're doing anyway, there's no way around it. Help them to build a wall of trust for you, but when you get it, don't let it fall down again! <br><br>[[Image:Be a Good Child Step 5.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "*If you are about to be punished, accept it. Don't complain. Tell your parent(s) that you are sorry and just try to do better in the future. There is no use arguing over it. If you say you're sorry (and mean it!), maybe the parent that is punishing you will lighten the load of punishment you get. You never know!",
                    "* Do chores for fun. That way, your parents will know you're a responsible child and that you are willing to help around the house.",
                    "*Always respect elders. If they scold you, apologize respectfully and avoid repeating the actions that you were scolded for.",
                    "* Never let your anger get to you. If you feel angry, do your best to control it and keep your cool. If worse comes to worst, you could even take a \"time out\" by retreating to your room and letting the steam out there."
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#'''[[Be Yourself|Be yourself]].''' Be you and be natural-Well, if you don't know the real you, just act naturally, the self you are most laid back and comfortable in.<br><br>[[Image:Be a Good Child Step 1.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Honor your parents. Don't lie to them, and don't do any sneaky stuff, because they know what you're doing anyway, there's no way around it. Help them to build a wall of trust for you, but when you get it, don't let it fall down again!<br><br>[[Image:Be a Good Child Step 5.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "*If you are about to be punished, accept it. Don't complain. Tell your parent(s) that you are sorry and just try to do better the second time. No use in arguing over it now. If you say you're sorry (and mean it!), maybe the parent that is punishing you will lighten the load of punishment you get. You never know!",
                    "*Always be kind.",
                    "*Be loyal and love them.",
                    "*Try to always do your best, don't forget that.",
                    "*Be happy.",
                    "*Don't yell at your parents a lot.",
                    "* Be good listen to your parents and teachers.",
                    "* Love your mother and father.",
                    "* Have a positive attitude.",
                    "* Don't talk back to your parents.",
                    "* Don't be disrespectful.",
                    "* Keep trying to do better, even if they tell you multiple times that you're not trying or not trying your very best.",
                    "* Do chores for fun. Your parents will know your a good child.<3.",
                    "* Be polite and do what your parents say and you will be rewarded.",
                    "* ALWAYS respect elders if they scold you say I am sorry.",
                    "* Never let your anger get to you.",
                    "",
                    "== Things You'll Need ==",
                    "*The ability to swallow your pride.",
                    "*Confidence"
                ]
            }
        },
