        {
            "id": "16974126",
            "user": "Isorhythmic",
            "timestamp": "21:21, 27 March 2015",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(3,300 bytes)",
            "change": -622,
            "summary": "(Reverted edits by Usernme (Talk); changed back to last version by Zack)",
            "is_minor": true,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "reverted",
            "contribution_type": "revert",
            "reverted_by": "LittleBeetles",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [],
                "removed": [
                    "* I know it's hard to get along with siblings, but think of it this way... There's no getting out of being related to them, and if your ways fighting, where's the fun? One day you won't have each other just across the hall, so cherish the moments you share and have fun with them, and try not to be the one that sparks the fight. It will be hard, but if you want to be happy you'll have to try it. Don't worry, your not the only one that has problems and arguments with your siblings. And the hardest part of allies is  forgiving and not thinking bad things about them. I know I should be nicer to my siblings and family."
                ]
            }
        },
